-- title:
--   Decode a physical wanted pair into incidence, lift, and block rows
-- statement:
--   Let a stored wanted slot contain natural indices $i,j\le V$, with incidence count $N>0$ and $j<c(h)^J$. Here $c(h)$ is the local output-key count. Assume the canonical layer-mask array is stored, both input regions end by destination $z$, and $z+4+2J\le f$. The decoder's space and word budgets must fit, space must fit in a word, and $d+3$ must be below the depth limit. With the specified division and output-decoding procedures installed, execution returns the occurrence-only code $q(j)$ and stores
--   $$
--   \mu'[z:z+4]=[i\bmod N,\lfloor i/N\rfloor,j,q(j)].
--   $$
--   The following two length-$J$ rows contain the decoded occurrence indices and original output masks. Memory below $z$ is preserved within the division-plus-decoding budget.
--
--   This connects a physical wanted pair to its retained source-bank occurrence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightWantedDecode.lean#L57-L164

